From c1db8862e2be9d3796c87a9a58895d71b08495a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ONYX <onyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:05:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] dzn: name the call after which the D3D12 device was
 removed

Xbox removes the device for invalid calls that return void or S_OK, so the
first failing call is far from the culprit. Every void D3D12 call, every
DZN_HR call and the start of most non-command entrypoints now check the
removed reason (each call while a game starts, then every 16th) and log the
call plus the 15 before it.
